hether t's __new__ is a class statement's (the first dictionary of its MRO holding __new__ is a"] [228 1 "// pyi class's, not a built-in's or a C type's): its tp_new is then CPython's slot_tp_new (Objects/typeobject.c,"] [229 1 "// type_new's tp_new for a class whose namespace defines __new__, which its subclasses inherit), the class's __new__"] [230 1 "// called, not its built-in base's (_pickle's load_newobj calls cls->tp_new: a list or tuple subclass's __new__,"] [231 1 "// test_descr's test_reduce_copying, a NamedTuple's, test_enum's tuple subclasses)."] [244 1 "// storeSlot writes the function fn into the slot id of the type object at a (its sub-struct's field when the type"] [245 1 "// has that sub-struct)."] [258 1 "// loadSlot reads the slot id of the type object at a (0: none, or no sub-struct)."] [271 1 "// ---- mirrors ----"] [273 1 "// mirror is the CPython layout of a tuple, list, bytes, float, int or str in the world's memory, a handle's."] [275 17 "// 't' tuple, 'l' list, 'b' bytes, 'f' float, 'i' int, 'u' str"] [276 17 "// the pyi object (a subclass's instance too: its built-in part is mirrored)"] [277 17 "// a tuple's or list's slots as last synchronized"] [278 17 "// a bytes' contents as last synchronized"] [279 17 "// the synchronization epoch of the last copy from C"] [280 2 "// a str's (queue 270, capi_unicode.go): its kind, ASCII flag and characters' address; a str PyUnicode_New made"] [281 2 "// (fresh) keeps a copy of its characters to see what C writes"] [290 2 "// held are the references mirrors hold on their items' handles because Go put the item there (a reference C"] [291 2 "// wrote into a slot is C's own): \"C holds the only reference\" (a brand-new object) is a count less these of 1"] [294 28 "// the mirrors a native (or a closure) used: synchronized to C when it returns"] [298 1 "// mirrorKind is the layout o's handle mirrors (0: a proxy's head only) and the bytes it needs."] [312 19 "// PyByteArrayObject (queue 270: PyByteArray_AS_S