her C holds the only reference to the handle h (its count, less the mirrors' own, is 1)."] [627 1 "// rawObj is the object a handle names without synchronizing it (nil for NULL)."] [636 1 "// freeMirror releases a mirror's own memory and its items' references (its handle released)."] [656 1 "// syncAllToC writes every mirror's pyi state into C (before the world is called: Python code may have changed any)."] [663 1 "// syncMutableToC writes the mutable mirrors' (a list's, a set's, a bytearray's) pyi state into C, C's own writes taken"] [664 1 "// first: a native that ran Python code returns (that code may have changed an object C reads in place, PyList_GET_SIZE's"] [665 1 "// ob_size: gh-92930's persistent_id clearing the list _pickle's batch_list_exact walks, test_pickle's"] [666 1 "// test_evil_pickler_mutating_collection)."] [670 26 "// released since"] [678 1 "// mutMirrors are the mutable mirrors syncMutableToC writes (a released one dropped as it meets it)."] [681 1 "// noteMutable records a new mirror among mutMirrors when its kind is mutable."] [689 1 "// syncAllFromC copies every mirror's C state to its pyi value (when the world returns to Python)."] [697 1 "// nativeEnter and nativeLeave bracket a native's (or a closure's) run: what C wrote is copied to Go on the first use"] [698 1 "// of a mirrored object in it (fromHandle), and the mirrors it used are written back to C when it returns."] [719 1 "// touch marks a mirrored handle as used by the running native."] [728 1 "// ---- C types over a built-in base (268's DECISION (a), the user 2026-11-11) ----"] [730 1 "// born is a C type's instance over a built-in base (a type a spec or PyType_Ready made, deriving from list, tuple,"] [731 1 "// bytes or float): its memory is the world's, tp_basicsize bytes (and its items'), the built-in part a mirror of the"] [732 1 "// pyi value at its head, the extension's part C's after the base's size. The Go value is an instance of the type"] [733 1 "// keeping a built-in value, as a Python class deriving from the built-in keeps one; the record rides on it"] [734 1 "// (py.SetInstanceExt). Its memory lives as a C-born object's (queue 268): until Go collects the instance, then its"] [735 1 "// tp_dealloc runs on the world's next entry."] [743 1 "// bornKind is the mirrored layout of t's built-in base (0: none of them)."] [756 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over int (its mirror a PyLongObject's)"] [759 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over an exception (no mirror: C reads its fields through functions)"] [765 1 "// bornOf is o's record when o is a C type's instance over a built-in base (nil: none)."] [777 1 "// bornHandle is such an instance's handle: its memory's address, in the maps again (a count of 0: unowned until the"] [778 1 "// C entry ends; its mirror written from Go, which may have changed it meanwhile) when it had left them."] [796 1 "// bornNew is tp_alloc for a C type over a built-in base: the instance of sub with nitems items (a tuple's or bytes'),"] [797 1 "// a new reference."] [824 1 "// bornValue is the built-in value of a C type's instance over a built-in base its base's __new__ makes from the"] [825 1 "// arguments (queue 270b: a spec over int without tp_new, HeapCTypeWithBasesSlot(5)): the base's own value, or for an"] [826 1 "// exception the exception of sub itself."] [846 1 "// bornWith makes the instance of sub keeping the built-in value v (for an exception, v is the instance), its memory"] [847 1 "// the world's: tp_basicsize bytes (and nitems items') or the mirror's size, the built-in part mirrored."] [896 1 "// allocObj is tp_alloc's generic allocation of t (PyType_GenericAlloc): a C-born object, an instance over a built-in"] [897 1 "// base, or a type object's memory (type's own tp_alloc: a heap type C fills, then PyType_Ready's)."] [900 3 "// a type object (a C metaclass's too, queue 270b: its basicsize, the C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject)"] [927 1 "// rawTypes are the type objects C allocated through type's tp_alloc